# apple

Backup of ping's Hyprland rice (configs only). Last refresh is in `BACKUP_TIME`.

## Layout

| Path | Goes to |
| --- | --- |
| `config/` | `~/.config/` |
| `home/` | `~/` (dotfiles) |
| `local-bin/` | `~/.local/bin/` |
| `local-share/fonts/` | `~/.local/share/fonts/` (Comfortaa for the lock screen) |

Copy those over, then `fc-cache -f` and log into Hyprland. `~/.local/bin` must be on `PATH`.

## Install packages

Chaotic-AUR is already used on this machine. If you do not have it, add it first or swap the chaotic lines for `yay -S`.

### pacman (extra / official)

```
sudo pacman -S --needed \
  hyprland hypridle hyprlock hyprsunset hyprpolkitagent \
  xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland xdg-desktop-portal-gtk \
  kitty ghostty \
  rofi nemo mako \
  playerctl brightnessctl grim slurp wl-clipboard \
  pipewire pipewire-pulse wireplumber pavucontrol \
  cava gtk4 gtk4-layer-shell gjs dart-sass \
  gobject-introspection npm python \
  inotify-tools imagemagick \
  ttf-iosevka-nerd ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd \
  bibata-cursor-theme noto-fonts \
  networkmanager bluez bluez-utils \
  starship fastfetch neovim \
  eza fzf zoxide yazi
```

### yay / chaotic-aur

AGS, wallpaper, theme, and the apps the binds launch:

```
yay -S --needed \
  aylurs-gtk-shell libastal-git libastal-4-git \
  awww matugen \
  firefox-developer-edition spotify
```

If chaotic-aur is already enabled, the same names work with `pacman -S`:

```
sudo pacman -S --needed \
  aylurs-gtk-shell libastal-git libastal-4-git \
  awww matugen \
  firefox-developer-edition spotify
```

`libastal-meta` is optional. This rice polls scripts instead of the extra Astal services.

## After install

1. `chmod +x ~/.local/bin/ags ~/.local/bin/hyprsunset ~/.config/ags/scripts/* ~/.config/hypr/scripts/*`
2. `systemctl --user enable --now wallpaper-watch.service hyprsunset.service`
3. Comfortaa is in `local-share/fonts`. Install those or `yay -S ttf-google-fonts-git` if you want it from a package.
4. Super+C control center, Super+H settings, Super+Shift+T wallpapers. Notifications stay with mako.

`local-bin/ags` is a wrapper. System `ags` from `aylurs-gtk-shell` is enough if `/usr/bin/ags` exists; the wrapper is there for a prefix install under `~/.local/opt/ags`.
